  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There appears to be a limit on the number of physbone colliders.  Once this limit is hit the log file is spammed with warnings about it at a rate that seems to depend on how many avatars.  Managed to get a 47GB log file before noticing.  After restarting I got a 600MB log file a few minutes after rejoining the map I was at.  \n\nThere was also noticeable worse performance in the map compared to events held at it prior to the physbone implementation, which might be tied to this considering the rate at which the warning is generating.\n\n\nexample log text:\n2022.04.24 02:42:11 Warning    -  PhysBoneManager::UpdateCollidersForChain - Max collider records\n2022.04.24 02:42:11 Warning    -  PhysBoneManager::UpdateCollidersForChain - Max collider records\n2022.04.24 02:42:11 Warning    -  PhysBoneManager::UpdateCollidersForChain - Max collider records\n2022.04.24 02:42:11 Warning    -  PhysBoneManager::UpdateCollidersForChain - Max collider records\n2022.04.24 02:42:11 Warning    -  PhysBoneManager::UpdateCollidersForChain - Max collider records\n2022.04.24 02:42:11 Warning    -  PhysBoneManager::UpdateCollidersForChain - Max collider records\n2022.04.24 02:42:11 Warning    -  PhysBoneManager::UpdateCollidersForChain - Max collider records\n2022.04.24 02:42:11 Warning    -  PhysBoneManager::UpdateCollidersForChain - Max collider records\n2022.04.24 02:42:11 Warning    -  PhysBoneManager::UpdateCollidersForChain - Max collider records\n2022.04.24 02:42:11 Warning    -  PhysBoneManager::UpdateCollidersForChain - Max collider records",
